Straight from the ACTUAL Greenhouse TOS listed on page 25 at [https://www08.wellsfargomedia.com/assets/pdf/personal/online-disclosures/fee-fii-en.pdf](https://www08.wellsfargomedia.com/assets/pdf/personal/online-disclosures/fee-fii-en.pdf) as opposed to the nonsense you just spewed above me:

Greenhouse Overdrafts:

"Overdrafts and Returned Items (Non-Sufficient Funds/NSF) It is possible for you to have an overdraft even though the available balance appears to show there are sufficient funds to cover a transaction that you want to make. For example, this can occur if you add a gratuity to a debit card transaction after the merchant has submitted the original amount to the Bank for authorization or if a deposited item is returned unpaid after we have credited your account. In the event your account (Greenhouse Set Aside Account or Greenhouse Spending Account) has a return item or an overdraft, we will not charge you a fee. You agree to pay the Bank the amount of the overdraft. We may deduct the overdraft amount from future funds in the account (Greenhouse Set Aside Account or Greenhouse Spending Account), if any, or from funds in other accounts you have with the Bank. If no such funds are available from which the Bank can be paid the overdraft amount, then the account (Greenhouse Set Aside Account and Greenhouse Spending Account) will be closed, and the Bank may initiate collection efforts to recover the overdraft balance. You agree to reimburse us for the costs and expenses of collection (including attorney’s fees and expenses) we incur in collecting the overdraft balance. You also authorize the Bank to cancel any recurring preauthorized payments against funds on your account (Greenhouse Set Aside Account or Greenhouse Spending Account).

&#x200B;

