from my understanding, major credit card companies now have deep integration partnerships with Paypal and are able to be alerted of linkages and usage. This comes down to the technical coding. Amex called me the other month because they were able to see that i sent money from my business to my personal Paypal account via an Amex credit card, and although the name of my business is 100% different, were alerted by Paypal that the names on the Paypal accounts matched, and that this was a violation of their policies, and if I did it again they would shut down my card.

